{# THE CONFIGURE FRAME A ROSTER SECTION WEARS.

   Each of this module's sections keeps an address of its own — it draws
   families the shell's sheet does not ship, and the shell's configure page
   links no module stylesheet — so each renders itself. What it must NOT do is
   look like a different page: it wears the configure page's heading, the
   configure page's section strip and the lit Configure action, all three drawn
   by the shell, and it draws no navigation and no way back of its own. The
   strip, the lit Configure and the crumb are the three ways back; there is no
   fourth.

   The heading and the summary are the ones RosterConfigurationSections
   declares, said here in the same words rather than a second wording of the
   same page. #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ area.name }} · Roster · configure{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}{{ area.name }} — Roster · configure{% endblock %}

{# THE SUBLINE IS THE PAGE'S, NOT THE FRAME'S. Each section says what IT is,
   in the design's own fragment, because a frame-wide sentence repeated on
   four pages is four pages that do not say where you are. The default below
   is for a section that has not overridden it. #}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}The cycles this area fills from &middot; the shifts and rules its stations run on &middot; configuration only, the figures live on the tabs{% endblock %}

{% block roster_trail_tail %} <a href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::OVERVIEW_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">roster</a> / configure{% endblock %}

{% block roster_page %}
    {{ include('@UhifadhiRoster/_identity_band.html.twig') }}
    {% block roster_section %}{% endblock %}
{% endblock %}
